 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_kr61x83",
   "entryDay": 41,
   "cause": "the expedition",
   "lines": [
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Jessica Dong is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d41: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d41: 🕯️ Jessica Dong is dead — the expedition. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d41: What Jessica kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d41: \"Jessica's gone.\" Wanjiru looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Jessica.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d41: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Diana blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Wound Care (Level 1). Clean it, close it, cover it. Pressure stops bleeding. Clean water is better than dirty hands.",
    "d41: ⚡ TECHNIQUE UNLOCKED: Precise Mend! Your healing knows where to go. +50% effectiveness. (Your knowledge of Wound Care amplifies your field_medicine.)",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Anatomy (Level 1). You know where the important bits are. Arteries, joints, organs. Useful for healing or hurting.",
    "d41: 📖 LEARNED: Calming Panic (Level 1). Ground them: 5 things you see, 4 you hear, 3 you touch. Breathe with them. Slow is fast.",
    "d41: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d41: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Jessica Dong, 41 days. The mantle passes to Diana Osei.",
    "d41: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Diana Osei, 26 — a paramedic. Her hands know different work now: Iron Stomach, Green Whisper, Berserker Rage, Beard Moss.",
    "d41: The village's quarrel was with Jessica — and Jessica is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d41: At the grave, Fernando, Zuri, Rashid and 3 more speak for Diana — \"Jessica trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d41: The fire knew Diana before the Codex did — her name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "diana_osei",
   "entryDay": 44,
   "cause": "a stranger",
   "lines": [
    "d44: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Diana Osei is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d44: 🕯️ Diana Osei is dead — a stranger. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d44: What Diana kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d44: \"Diana's gone.\" Fernando looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Diana.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d44: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Wanjiru blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d44: 📖 LEARNED: Scrounger (Level 1). Ruin looting finds +1 item.",
    "d44: 📖 LEARNED: Herbal Medicine (Level 1). Willow bark = aspirin. Yarrow stops bleeding. Plantain draws out infection. The pharmacy is outside.",
    "d44: 📖 LEARNED: Wire Snares (Level 1). A loop of wire on a game trail. Simple, effective, ancient. Check at dawn.",
    "d44: 📖 LEARNED: Reading the Land (Level 1). Eat the landscape with your eyes first: green + water + sun means food grows here. Start where those three meet.",
    "d44: 📖 LEARNED: The Forager’s Eye (Level 1). You walk slower and see more. Food was always there; now you notice it.",
    "d44: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d44: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Diana Osei, 44 days. The mantle passes to Wanjiru Kamau.",
    "d44: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Wanjiru Kamau, 30 — a Wild food forager. Her hands know different work now: Night Eyes, Lucky Rock.",
    "d44: At the grave, Fernando, Zuri, Rashid and 2 more speak for Wanjiru — \"Diana trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d44: The fire knew Wanjiru before the Codex did — her name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "wanjiru_kamau",
   "entryDay": 75,
   "cause": "a stranger",
   "lines": [
    "d75: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Wanjiru Kamau is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d75: 🕯️ Wanjiru Kamau is dead — a stranger. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d75: What Wanjiru kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d75: \"Wanjiru's gone.\" Fernando looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Wanjiru.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d75: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Zuri blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d75: 📖 LEARNED: Diplomatic Incident (Level 1). Trust builds 2x faster. You're TOO good though — once per week you can start a diplomatic incident: villagers argue, you pick the winner (+trust with them, -trust with the loser).",
    "d75: 📖 LEARNED: Mediation (Level 1). Let each side talk without interruption. Repeat back what you heard. People de-escalate when heard.",
    "d75: The warm hum behind your ribs is gone. The reactor went with Wanjiru's body — it does not come out, and it does not pass on. Hunger is back on the table. (One reactor per world, and the world already spent its one.)",
    "d75: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d75: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Wanjiru Kamau, 75 days. The mantle passes to Zuri Jankowski.",
    "d75: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Zuri Jankowski, 34 — a comic shop owner. Their hands know different work now: The Touch, Scream Cheese, Lucky Rock.",
    "d75: The village's quarrel was with Wanjiru — and Wanjiru is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d75: You knew Wanjiru — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting her, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d75: At the grave, Fernando, Milagros, Olivia and 3 more speak for Zuri — \"Wanjiru trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d75: The fire knew Zuri before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  }
 ],
